# TT1: TIMED arm A of the paired ABAB on coding prompts (audits off): A = c2-packed-tp4-best-ship (control), B = c2-packed-tp4-best-ship-tpub (the traced carry copies); the pair differs in QWEN_FAST_TP4_TRACED_PUBLISH alone (test_tp4_next5).
# Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order. Runs only if T1, T2 and T3 passed (NEEDS in ORDER.txt). The tests: warmup, coding and long_real_text
# (the lone-user sequential steps the lever speeds up) and concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k: the lever must cost nothing there).
# READ: the lone-user step lines '[SEQ-PUBLISH] request= rows= prefix= step_ms=' (about 75 ms at rows=4 today; the arm target about 15 ms less) and the carry save lines '[CARRY] op=save ... enqueue_ms='
# (B logs traced=1 on them; the eager save's ~16 ms host should drop), and the '[PACKED-PHASE]' lines of the four-user test (unchanged within noise). Judge the arms PAIRED per step and per round,
# never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run and repeat before believing a small gap. No CI pushes while a timed arm runs (CI shares the host).
# Exactness offline: compare the two SMOKE_JSON results test by test and user by user (warmup, coding, long_real_text, concurrent4_code_equal users 0-3): content_sha256, reasoning_sha256,
# completion_tokens and finish must be identical A against B. (speed_window_compare reads matrix-gate trees, which a smoke job does not write.) Duration (estimate): 60 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4_code_equal
